In this section, we define the factorization homology of $\cB$-manifolds with coefficients in $\disk(\cB)$-algebras, and we verify some of the essential properties of this construction. It is a symmetric monoidal functor from $\cB$-manifolds and embeddings.

For this section we fix:
\begin{itemize}
\item a symmetric monoidal $\infty$-category $\cV$ that is $\ot$-sifted cocomplete,
\item an $\oo$-category of basics $\cB = (\cB \to \bsc)$.
\end{itemize}

Factorization homology will have a universal property with respect to monoidal and operadic structures on $\mfld(\cB)$ and $\mfld(\cB)_{/X}$, which we present below in Constructions \ref{B-monoidals} and \ref{B-operadics}.

